pagate end-to-end. This is not explained by volume (only 2186 events, repeat ratio 0.004), by hub brokerage (all relays have 2-5 partners; the local hub 1566 is off-path), or by time-ignored connectivity (the 2-hop neighbourhoods of source and target are disjoint)."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Static path discovery.** The 2-hop neighbourhoods of 1885 (step_03) and 1460 (step_05) are *disjoint*, so any influence must travel further. Expanding to 3 hops from 1460 (step_06) plus 1885's neighbourhood reveals exactly one directed chain, and every hop points the right way:\n\n`1885 \u2192 749 \u2192 1453 \u2192 1871 \u2192 632 \u2192 1460`\n\n**Temporal localisation.** Coarse 600-unit binning (steps 09\u201314) shows all six nodes fire in a single narrow burst, in staircase order:\n\n| event | time bin |\n|---|---|\n| 1885 \u2192 749 | [22283, 22882] (1885's *only* event in the whole 9600-unit window) |\n| 749 \u2192 1453 | [22583, 22682] (step_15) |\n| 1453 \u2192 1871 | one of A=[22883,22982], B=[23183,23282], C=[23383,23482] |\n| 1871 \u2192 632 | one of A/B/C |\n| 632 \u2192 1460 | one of A/B/C |\n\nFine 100-unit binning (steps 15, 16) resolves the tail: the three remaining hops occupy the three bins A, B, C with exactly one event each \u2014 1453/632 activity and 1871/1460 activity land on the identical bins, which is only consistent with the three chain events being spread one per bin. Every consecutive gap is then \u2264 ~500 units, comfortably inside the 600-unit latency budget, and the whole cascade completes in ~900 units.\n\n**Confounder controls.**\n- *Volume:* the window holds only 2186 events over 1500 active nodes with repeat_ratio 0.0037 (step_01) \u2014 essentially one event per node, so this dense 1200-unit co-occurrence of six path-adjacent nodes is not a background-rate artefact.\n- *Hub/popularity explanation:* the relays are low-degree, not hubs \u2014 749 has 5 partners, 1453 has 2, 632 has 4, 252 has 1 (step_08). The one genuine hub in the region (1566, 58 partners) is *not* on the path, so the connection is not manufactured by a popular broker.\n- *Time-ignored connectivity:* explicitly ruled out as sufficient \u2014 the static 2-hop check (steps 03, 05) showed no shortcut, and the 4-hop expansion (step_04) confirms 1885 reaches a large component, yet the decision rests on the ordered bin sequence, not mere reachability.\n\nResidual uncertainty: the bin resolution leaves the internal ordering of the final three hops not fully pinned, hence confidence below 0.9.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_5bd75546\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 749, 1453, 1871, 632, 1460],\n  \"window\": [18083, 27683],\n  \"confidence\": 0.76,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A fully directed chain 1885->749->1453->1871->632->1460 exists and its events are tightly clustered in [22283,23482]: 1885's sole event fires in [22283,22882], the 749-1453 hop at 22583-22682, and the final three hops occupy one each of the 100-unit bins [22883,22982], [23183,23282], [23383,23482]. All consecutive gaps are under 600 units, so influence could propagate end-to-end. This is not explained by volume (only 2186 events, repeat ratio 0.004), by hub brokerage (all relays have 2-5 partners; the local hub 1566 is off-path), or by time-ignored connectivity (the 2-hop neighbourhoods of source and target are disjoint).\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 40594, "total_output_tokens": 11401, "total_tokens": 51995, "total_latency_ms": 142015, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}